# The pinned fx's own surface inventory, read off its screens: the /help menu
# and the slash popup, each walked from end to start, at the sweep's size.
# inventory.py reads the snaps back. Not a parity scenario: it lives outside
# scenarios/, so the sweep never runs it.
#
# Each walk starts with one Up from the first row, which wraps to the last
# row and shows the menu's tail, and goes on up five rows a page. Going up, a
# window's top row is the selected one, so five rows a page never skips a row
# in a window of six or more; going down, a step can wrap past a tail it never
# showed (a first version of this file missed /mcp../trace that way).
# inventory.py checks the rows read against the menu's own `Commands N`, so a
# short read fails instead of shrinking the count.
wait 2.5
type /help
key Enter
wait 1.2
snap help-00
key Up
wait 0.5
snap help-01
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-02
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-03
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-04
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-05
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-06
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
snap help-07
key Up Up Up Up Up
wait 0.4
